<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="dark"><title>Sentiment Radar — 2026-09-23</title><style>:root{color-scheme:dark}*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#0b1320;color:#e7effb;font:15px/1.65 'Segoe UI',Arial,sans-serif}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:30px 24px}a{color:#83b4ff}h1{font-size:34px;line-height:1.15}h2{margin-top:36px;font-size:24px}h3{margin:6px 0 12px;font-size:22px}p{margin:10px 0}.muted,.sources{color:#a9b9cc}.sources{font-size:12px}.eyebrow{color:#8bdac8;text-transform:uppercase;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1px}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:16px}article,.market{padding:22px;background:#142033;border:1px solid #304258;border-radius:14px}article{margin:12px 0}.metrics{padding:12px 14px;background:#0b1729;border-left:3px solid #7e9dff;font-size:13px}details{padding:14px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #304258}summary{cursor:pointer}blockquote{color:#b5c7dc;border-left:3px solid #37557a;margin:12px 0;padding-left:16px}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #304258;text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}.scroll{overflow:auto}footer{margin:32px 0;color:#9bafc8;font-size:13px}@media(max-width:750px){.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}main{padding:22px 14px}h1{font-size:28px}}</style><style id="dashboard-dark-theme">:root{color-scheme:dark}body{background:#0b1320;color:#e7effb}::selection{background:#345d8c;color:#fff}select,input,button{color-scheme:dark}a:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,select:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #79adff;outline-offset:3px}</style></head><body><nav aria-label="Wiki navigation" style="background:#101c2e;color:#a6b7ce;border-bottom:1px solid #2d4059;padding:10px 24px;font:14px Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif"><a href="../index.html" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">← Wiki dashboards</a><span style="margin:0 12px">/</span><a href="index.html" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">Sentiment Radar</a><span style="margin:0 12px">/</span><a href="http://DS-CAP-33:8080/dashboards/#sentiment-radar" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">Main dashboards</a><span style="margin:0 12px">/</span><a href="daily-brief.html" style="color:#79adff;text-decoration:none">Daily briefing</a></nav><main><p><a href="index.html">All dashboards</a> · <a href="http://DS-CAP-33:8080/dashboards/#sentiment-radar">Main hub</a></p><div class="eyebrow">Daily review · 2026-09-23</div><h1>Consumer-agent enthusiasm is spreading; several winners already carry crowded expectations.</h1><p>META has stronger cross-desk crowding warnings; LITE combines a fresh crowding comment with more vendor mentions. MRVL and CRDO show why price, mention volume and desk conviction need separate readings.</p><p class="muted">Prices/vendor X: 22 Sep · Selected original-post windows: through 21 Sep · Emails: through 2026-09-23T13:04:45.4131923Z</p><div class="market"><h2 style="margin-top:0">Fear &amp; Greed: 35.1/100</h2><p>CNN Fear &amp; Greed is 35.1/100 (fear), timestamp 2026-09-23T12:49:16+00:00. No new entry into our &lt;=30/20 or &gt;=70/80 extreme zones. The 15 September &lt;=30 entry now has a complete five-session outcome through 22 September: SPY +2.36%, QQQ +6.20% (gross total return, reading-date close to t+5 close; descriptive timing).</p><p>Editorial watchlists below combine source content with quantitative context. They are not a score ranking or measured fund holdings.</p></div><section><h2>More positive / more crowded</h2><div class="grid"><article><div class="eyebrow">Crowded optimism</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=META">META</a></h3><p>JPM describes unusually unanimous enthusiasm and says META would rank at the top of its hedge-fund positioning axis. UBS sees little pushback despite event expectations. Jefferies agrees that HF positioning leans very long, while questioning how much of the move reflects long-only buying.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +9.9%; X vendor mentions 389 → 435 / five sessions; tone 0.002; attention score 88.6/100 (+9.9 since prior delivery). Selected X: 64 posts / 29 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> The 21 September review already identified a popular HF long with thin long-only sponsorship. Today adds a stronger cross-desk warning about expectations; it does not establish a new ownership percentage.</p><details><summary>What to watch · High for desk consensus; holdings unverified</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch whether Connect announcements meet the elevated product and monetization bar; an enthusiastic reaction alone is not evidence of incremental long-only demand.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Look for sustained third-party adoption, monetization evidence and identifiable new buyers after the event.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-7923838d9822">JPMorgan / Mark Schilsky (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-3aead40bc64b">UBS / Christina Dwyer (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-4f5d8a0e4ac2">Jefferies / Joseph Favuzza (2026-09-23)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">Optics narrative becoming crowded</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=LITE">LITE</a></h3><p>Barclays calls LITE the preferred optics expression and increasingly crowded on the long side. Redburn relays new ECOC optical demonstrations, a technical catalyst that is distinct from investor-positioning evidence.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +12.7%; X vendor mentions 38 → 73 / five sessions; tone 0.089; attention score 82.2/100 (+6.5 since prior delivery). Selected X: 5 posts / 3 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> The previous JPM/UBS review was already constructive and flagged high expectations. A new house now explicitly describes crowding, while vendor mention activity is rising.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; thin selected X sample</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Check whether ECOC and CPO/NPO news keep attracting new participants after the rally.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Look for commercial timelines and broader independent-author participation; recurring promotional or relayed posts alone would weaken the signal.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-17b23deeed92">Rothschild &amp; Co / Rowan Adley (2026-09-22)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">CPU enthusiasm spreading</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=AMD">AMD</a></h3><p>Barclays describes a preferred long across short- and long-term investors; Bernstein reports positive CPU-trade feedback. The agent narrative now carries a material valuation and expectations hurdle after the price move.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +23.7%; X vendor mentions 720 → 1,764 / five sessions; tone 0.147; attention score 96.3/100 (+15.8 since prior delivery). Selected X: 39 posts / 19 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> Vendor mentions and the attention score strengthened since the prior report. This is confirmation of adoption of the narrative, not a still-undiscovered idea.</p><details><summary>What to watch · High for attention; medium for positioning</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch participation and relative performance after the sharp move; avoid counting short covering as proof of new conviction.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Test whether CPU demand and the GPU ramp translate into orders and estimate revisions.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-0fbacd8bb081">Bernstein / Tyler Seidman (2026-09-22)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">Positive event expectations; uneven breadth</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=MRVL">MRVL</a></h3><p>Barclays sees investors leaning positive into the analyst day on the Google/TPU opportunity, especially relative to AVGO. Collected X discussion is concentrated and vendor five-session mentions are below the preceding window.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +18.3%; X vendor mentions 655 → 616 / five sessions; tone 0.048; attention score 52.5/100 (+12.7 since prior delivery). Selected X: 21 posts / 5 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> The desk narrative remains constructive and the score rose from the last delivery, but mention volume does not confirm broad acceleration. Keep this divergence visible.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Separate new customer or program information from repeated analyst-day anticipation.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Compare actual disclosed opportunity, ramp timing and margin economics with the increasingly optimistic expectations.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">New narrative gaining inbound interest</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=SHOP">SHOP</a></h3><p>Bernstein explicitly reports a significant rise in SHOP inbound inquiries and sees the Muse integration as a position of strength. Jefferies asks whether partnership-driven gains can persist. Redburn raises a longer-term question about payment-button economics.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +13.8%; X vendor mentions 282 → 326 / five sessions; tone 0.003; attention score 75.9/100 (+23.1 since prior delivery). Selected X: 5 posts / 5 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> This is a fresh demand-for-discussion signal from specialist sales, with price and vendor mentions also rising. The small selected X sample limits breadth conclusions.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; sparse selected X sample</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch follow-through after the partnership announcement and new independent investors joining the discussion.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Test conversion, merchant adoption and take-rate economics; integration headlines alone cannot establish durable value capture.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-c3a6dd6b48a4">Bernstein / Tyler Seidman (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-4f5d8a0e4ac2">Jefferies / Joseph Favuzza (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-f9e1e2bd69db">Rothschild &amp; Co / Rowan Adley (2026-09-23)</a></p></article></div></section><section><h2>Weaker conviction / bearish positioning</h2><div class="grid"><article><div class="eyebrow">Crowded short — squeeze risk</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=AVGO">AVGO</a></h3><p>Barclays calls AVGO one of the more crowded tactical shorts on share-loss and margin concerns. Bernstein relays a constructive fundamental view from Stacy Rasgon. This is bearish positioning context with squeeze risk, not a uniform negative thesis.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +7.4%; X vendor mentions 253 → 208 / five sessions; tone 0.022; attention score 38.6/100 (+1.9 since prior delivery). Selected X: 9 posts / 6 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> The current desk comment confirms an unfavorable near-term narrative; price and vendor tone are positive, so the signals disagree.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; desk/research disagreement</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch positive customer or margin surprises that could challenge crowded shorts.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Evaluate ASIC share and margin evidence; keep tactical positioning separate from the fundamental analyst view.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-0fbacd8bb081">Bernstein / Tyler Seidman (2026-09-22)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">Consensus short returning</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=QCOM">QCOM</a></h3><p>Barclays says QCOM has returned to consensus-short status, with less CPU enthusiasm than AMD/INTC/ARM and the data-center story still needing proof.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +5.6%; X vendor mentions 1,382 → 569 / five sessions; tone 0.033; attention score 49.2/100 (+8.9 since prior delivery). Selected X: 17 posts / 12 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> This differs from the earlier covering discussion in the retained review. Five-session vendor mention activity fell; the latest daily score rebound does not erase that longer-window cooling.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; one fresh desk assessment</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch data-center announcements and whether short positioning produces squeezes rather than lasting sponsorship.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Seek design-win, timing and earnings evidence strong enough to offset smartphone concerns.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">Desk conviction weaker despite price strength</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=CRDO">CRDO</a></h3><p>Barclays reports more caution around the AEC business despite continued optimism on optics. The stock has risen strongly, making the divergence between price and desk conviction the useful observation.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +28.0%; X vendor mentions 529 → 514 / five sessions; tone 0.057; attention score 60.5/100 (+0.9 since prior delivery). Selected X: 8 posts / 2 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> The new comment flags a higher burden of proof for beats and raises. Neither positive price momentum nor a modestly higher score resolves the AEC debate.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; concentrated X coverage</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch whether AEC news supports the rally and whether discussion spreads beyond the dominant selected author.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Test the magnitude of order growth and earnings revisions rather than treating optics enthusiasm as proof for the entire business.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">Tactical enthusiasm cooling</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=AMZN">AMZN</a></h3><p>Jefferies reports some tactical short interest in AMZN and feedback that its sentiment placement should be lower. UBS still sees durable logistics, fulfillment and transaction advantages despite concern about consumer agents.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d +2.6%; X vendor mentions 1,329 → 1,139 / five sessions; tone -0.002; attention score 64.8/100 (+10.8 since prior delivery). Selected X: 36 posts / 24 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> This is a shift from the earlier widely-owned bullish expectations described in the 21 September review. The new evidence is reported investor feedback, not measured fund outflows.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; not evidence of broad selling</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch the debate over Muse access, sponsored discovery and retail economics.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Check whether ad monetization, transaction ownership and AWS evidence change the balance of the thesis.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-4f5d8a0e4ac2">Jefferies / Joseph Favuzza (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-3aead40bc64b">UBS / Christina Dwyer (2026-09-23)</a></p></article><article><div class="eyebrow">Weakening sentiment with quantitative confirmation</div><h3><a href="crowding-tracker.html#ticker=RDDT">RDDT</a></h3><p>Jefferies reports agreement with a downgrade in RDDT sentiment; JPM includes RDDT in the consumer-agent vulnerability basket discussion. Vendor tone and the latest price move are negative.</p><div class="metrics">Price 5d -2.5%; X vendor mentions 421 → 314 / five sessions; tone -0.092; attention score 26.1/100 (+2.4 since prior delivery). Selected X: 2 posts / 2 authors.</div><p><b>Change:</b> Desk caution now lines up with deteriorating five-session vendor tone. Low selected-feed coverage means the independent-author evidence is still weak.</p><details><summary>What to watch · Medium; sparse original-post sample</summary><p><b>1–5 sessions:</b> Watch whether agent-disintermediation headlines continue to dominate and whether price stabilizes despite them.</p><p><b>2–4 weeks:</b> Test traffic, engagement and monetization evidence. Stabilization in those metrics could make this a neglected-name recovery candidate.</p></details><p class="sources"><a href="#source-4f5d8a0e4ac2">Jefferies / Joseph Favuzza (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-7923838d9822">JPMorgan / Mark Schilsky (2026-09-23)</a></p></article></div></section><section><h2>Quality-source notes</h2><article><h3>Cyber: quality of evidence before tweet volume</h3><p>Fernanda Watkins forwarded the 22 September Susquehanna expert-call recap. The expert favors PANW and ZS, is cautious on FTNT and AKAM, and is neutral on CHKP and NET. This supports company-specific work on platformization and AI demand; it is one expert recap, not a survey of investor positioning. PANW has only two non-wire posts from two authors in the selected seven-day X feed. The Barclays cyber email is a request for survey responses, not results.</p><p class="sources"><a href="#source-c8618a0e098a">Fernanda Watkins (2026-09-22)</a> · <a href="#source-89ec327ac8e9">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-22)</a></p></article><article><h3>Memory/CPUs: distinguish short covering from new longs</h3><p>UBS Ruple describes the memory rebound as accompanied by short covering and perhaps a Muse boost, while fundamental MU checks remain constructive. Barclays believes most INTC shorts have already gone away. Neither statement quantifies new long buying. These are useful contrasts to price strength.</p><p class="sources"><a href="#source-004bdb95a1bd">UBS / Robert Ruple (2026-09-23)</a> · <a href="#source-91d153d89928">Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23)</a></p></article><article><h3>Damnang: a new technical lead, with a long adoption horizon</h3><p>The 23 September HBM hybrid-bonding expert interview emphasizes height, thermal performance, process integration and production experience. The expert frames 2026–2030 as a transition period and distinguishes Besi logic-bonding experience from eventual HBM equipment selection. Treat this as semiconductor-process research; it is not direct evidence of new LITE demand or investor crowding. No fresh SemiAnalysis company thesis was identified in the targeted priority-email screen.</p><p class="sources"><a href="#source-1048bc6e5e71">Damnang (2026-09-23)</a></p></article></section><h2>Next-week returns after new extreme entries</h2><div class="scroll"><table><thead><tr><th>Threshold</th><th>Events</th><th>SPY mean</th><th>SPY up</th><th>QQQ mean</th><th>QQQ up</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>≤20</td><td>19</td><td>+0.22%</td><td>58%</td><td>+0.22%</td><td>47%</td></tr><tr><td>≤30</td><td>38</td><td>+0.67%</td><td>74%</td><td>+1.14%</td><td>68%</td></tr><tr><td>≥70</td><td>20</td><td>+0.07%</td><td>55%</td><td>+0.15%</td><td>45%</td></tr><tr><td>≥80</td><td>5</td><td>-0.20%</td><td>40%</td><td>-0.48%</td><td>40%</td></tr><tr><td>≥90</td><td>0</td><td>N/A%</td><td>N/A%</td><td>N/A%</td><td>N/A%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="muted">Close on reading date to t+5 close; gross total return. Same-threshold holding windows do not overlap. Both <=30 mean confidence intervals include zero; >=80 has only five events, >=90 has none. Historical association, not an executable strategy. <a href="cnn-next-week.html">Explore intervals and timing sensitivity</a>.</p><h2>Sources and short evidence anchors</h2><details id="source-7923838d9822"><summary>JPMorgan / Mark Schilsky (2026-09-23) · JPM TECH SKETCH: META No Watermelon at Connect, Agentic AI Loser Baskets Raging (re: NYT, EXPE, CART), SPOT Q4 GM Concerns, EXPE/CART on META Muse</summary><p>Received 2026-09-23T12:09:36Z · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B4BB28E0000">Original email</a></p><blockquote>META would undoubtedly be a 10 on the hedge fund axis</blockquote><blockquote>NYT, CART, RDDT, RKT</blockquote></details><details id="source-3aead40bc64b"><summary>UBS / Christina Dwyer (2026-09-23) · UBS TMI: 09/23/2026: META Connect - What to Expect + Who to Watch? EXPE, CRWV Initiation, AI Colocation Launch (HUT, WULF, APLD, CORZ &amp; CIFR), Ad Check #1 Feedback (+), Ad Check #2 TODAY @ 10AM ET, FRMI, Key Events, Headlines, Access &amp; More</summary><p>Received 2026-09-23T11:41:31Z · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B170BCF0000">Original email</a></p><blockquote>how little pushback I fielded</blockquote><blockquote>AMZN remains well positioned even in this agentic frenzy</blockquote></details><details id="source-4f5d8a0e4ac2"><summary>Jefferies / Joseph Favuzza (2026-09-23) · Jefferies Tech: Internet Positioning, Muse Partnerships, Everything&#x27;s An AI Loser Update, ON NDR Takes, SAP Q3 Preview, Calls to Know</summary><p>Received 2026-09-23T11:37:43Z · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B170BCC0000">Original email</a></p><blockquote>HF positioning skewed very long META</blockquote><blockquote>can actually see follow through</blockquote><blockquote>tactical lean is more short in AMZN</blockquote><blockquote>No pushback on RDDT having a downtick</blockquote></details><details id="source-91d153d89928"><summary>Barclays / Jeffrey Rand (2026-09-23) · Barclays TMT Desk Commentary: Cybersecurity Sentiment Survey; Semis – Company 1-2 liners; PATH - takeaways from Analyst Day; S&amp;P 500 and Nasdaq-100 Projected Additions; BABA – 11 Highlights from Apsara Conference</summary><p>Received 2026-09-23T11:21:01Z · <a href="outlook:00000000B631393D2F642040B19B70F93F8427620700C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00000000010C0000C1A4BC1B9694F44D9FADFEFCFB028EAC00058B170BBF0000">Original email</a></p><blockquote>LITE seems to be the preferred wa